    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32570" root="غو or غوى" body-key="g">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَوًى</span></b>  <i>Thirst.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And one says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِتُّ غَوًى</span>,
and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَوِيًّا</span></b> , and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُغْوِيًا</span></b> , (K, TA,) in the T ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُغَوًّى</span></b> ,
(TA,) [in the CK <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَغْوِيًّا</span>,] meaning <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُخْلِيًا</span> (K, TA)
[in the CK <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُخَلَّيًا</span>] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُوحِشًا</span> (TA) [i. e. <i>I passed the
night empty</i>]: and so <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَوِيًا</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَاوِيًا</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُقْوِيًا</span>.
(TA.) [See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَوِىٌّ</span>.]

